G35.amended_change:
(1) Signs. Six doorways get a still sign drawn on the picture (not a button). These are the foyer stairs ⬆️🛏️, the landing stair top ⬇️🏠, the den stairs ⬆️🏠, the backyard back door ⬇️🛋️, the den Dutch door ⬆️🦌, and the foyer basement doorway, whose existing bobbing ⬇️ gets 🛋️ drawn beside it. A sign is drawn only where every point of its box would do exactly what tapping that door does today:
- the sign box lies inside the door's own hit box, below its top edge (aim for T + 30–46, as basement.js:139 does);
- hitTest(x, y) returns that same door or stairs prop at the box centre and corners (so no person, mess, wall picture or other prop is in front);
- exitSignHit(x, y) is null, and the box is more than 14 world units from the view's left and right edges between y 38 and 150, where the wall exit tabs and the deer/turkey tabs take taps first;
- no part is under the HUD: hudRects() plus #roombar .rb, #moodbar .mood, #moodToggle and #mapBtn.
If no such spot exists in that frame, the sign is not drawn. Cache the HUD rects for 250 ms instead of reading them every frame. Wrap drawExitSigns once at load and never re-wrap: builder.js:234 will wrap it again on the next frame, and the signs then draw before builder's late drawing, which is fine.
(2) Edge tab, only in the bathroom, the spa and the tree houses, and only while the way out is off-screen. The tab is placed at the view edge on that side, at a height where the whole tab box has hitTest() null and no button, face card, ✋, 📒/👗, wish or request is over it. Prefer the floor band (y 150–168), where a tap today already walks her toward that side. The spot is re-checked at least every 250 ms, not cached per screen shape. The tab is hidden while G.busy, G.sceneOn, G.tidy or G.chase is set, while marina.state is bars, swing or tantrum, or while any screen is open. On tap, the overlay's onTap wrapper takes the tap only when all of these hold: the tab is drawn, the point is inside it, !G.busy, and hitTest at the tap point is null. Every other tap goes to the original onTap unchanged. When it takes the tap, it runs the same steps as the exit-sign tap at features.js:381-385:
- UI.closeActions();
- reset perch, sit, cheer and sad to idle;
- mover = marina.mount || marina;
- Audio2.blip(9, 'triangle', 0.05, 0.1);
- mover.walkTo(exit.x ± 20, null, marina.mount ? 75 : null, FLOOR).
What each door does, its landing spot and the 🪜/💺 choices are unchanged.

G16.reason:
This survives refutation. The misfires are real taps:
- 3 of 3 fridge taps opened the sticker book (crit/five-year-old/triple_port_kitchen_fridge_1.png);
- monkey bars and the front door opened the book in the first-minutes sessions;
- a tap on Daddy's chest opened it too.
To a non-reader, a grid of grey '?' tiles has no link to the fridge she tapped.

I injected the draft CSS (verify/hud-child/g16.js, shots/g16_*.png). In port, portSmall, 390x664 and the notch app:
- the buttons land between the face cards with 0 px² overlap with the cards, the moods and a showing request;
- elementFromPoint at each centre returns the button;
- there is a 55-200 px gap above the moods.

The habit cost is real but modest. The new spot is high-contrast in an otherwise empty band, the same 1.5 s idle rule applies, and nothing in the scene can sit under the buttons any more.

One flaw: the glide bridge animates the buttons across the picture from their old spot. While they are tappable mid-flight, they can catch exactly the scene tap this item is meant to stop. Also note that short portrait (375x553, Safari on a small phone) fails min-height:150vw and keeps today's spot over the picture (measured).

